<!-- Phase 1: Base Case
Start Time: 0 seconds

Network: Normal operation. Global network delay is 0ms, and packet loss is 0%.

PBFT/Agent: Normal operation. All fault injections (proposal delays, dirty reports, ignore reports) are commented out or disabled.

Phase 2: Small Proposal Delay (Leader)
Start Time: 100 seconds

Network: Normal operation (0ms delay, 0% loss).

PBFT: A small proposal delay of 300ms is applied specifically to the current leader node.

Phase 3: Continued Small Proposal Delay (Leader)
Start Time: 200 seconds

Network: Normal operation.

PBFT: Maintains the 300ms proposal delay for the leader node.

Phase 4: Continued Small Proposal Delay (Leader)
Start Time: 300 seconds

Network: Normal operation.

PBFT: Maintains the 300ms proposal delay for the leader node.

Phase 5: Large Proposal Delay (Replica 0)
Start Time: 400 seconds

Network: Normal operation.

PBFT: The fault target shifts. A large proposal delay of 900ms is applied specifically to Replica 0.

Phase 6: Continued Large Proposal Delay (Replica 0)
Start Time: 500 seconds

Network: Normal operation.

PBFT: Maintains the 900ms proposal delay for Replica 0.

Phase 7: Continued Large Proposal Delay (Replica 0)
Start Time: 600 seconds

Network: Normal operation.

PBFT: Maintains the 900ms proposal delay for Replica 0.

Phase 8: Small Network Delay
Start Time: 700 seconds

Network: A small global network delay of 50ms is introduced across all directed edges.

PBFT: Proposal delays are deactivated (back to normal).

Phase 9: Small Network Delay + Small Proposal Delay
Start Time: 1300 seconds

Network: Maintains the global 50ms network delay.

PBFT: Reintroduces a small proposal delay of 300ms specifically for Replica 0.

Phase 10: Continued Network & Proposal Delays
Start Time: 1900 seconds

Network: Maintains the global 50ms network delay.

PBFT: Maintains the 300ms proposal delay for Replica 0.

Phase 11: Continued Network & Proposal Delays
Start Time: 2500 seconds

Network: Maintains the global 50ms network delay.

PBFT: Maintains the 300ms proposal delay for Replica 0.

Phase 12: Large Network Delay
Start Time: 3100 seconds

Network: A large global network delay of 150ms is introduced across all directed edges.

PBFT: Proposal delays are deactivated once again.
 -->